# apps/api/Dockerfile does `COPY apps/api ./apps/api`, which would otherwise pull
# apps/api/.env -- the hosted DATABASE_URL (with its password), the hosted service-role key
# and the paid Gemini key -- into the build context and the build stage's filesystem.
#
# The published image happens to be clean anyway: the runtime stage copies only
# package.json, node_modules and dist from the build stage. This file exists so that stays a
# fact rather than a coincidence -- one `COPY --from=build /repo/apps/api` in a future
# refactor would bake real credentials into a layer, and nothing else in the repo would
# notice. Every one of these values is supplied by the deploy target at runtime; none belongs in an
# image.
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Never needed by the build, and the largest thing in the upload.
.git
**/node_modules

# Build output is produced inside the image; shipping a host-built copy in risks a stale
# dist/ shadowing the one `nest build` creates.
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/.expo
